<title>GERMANY: TENNIS-GERMAN OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-GERMAN OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the German Open men's tennis tournament on Wednesday (prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>Alex Radulescu (Germany) beat Tomas Nydahl (Sweden) 4-6 7-6 (7-4) 7-5</p>
<p>10-Felix Mantilla (Spain) beat Magnus Larsson (Sweden) 6-7 (2-7) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Roberto Carretero (Spain) beat Jens Knippschild (Germany) 4-6 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Carlos Costa (Spain) beat Daniel Elsner (Germany) 7-6 (9-7) 6-3</p>
<p>Oliver Gross (Germany) beat Karim Alami (Morocco) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>11-Alberto Berasategui (Spain) beat Arnaud Boetsch (France) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Magnus Gustafsson (Sweden) beat Cedric Pioline (France) 6-4 1-6 6-3</p>
<p>Christian Ruud (Norway) beat Mikael Tillstrom (Sweden) 6-1 4-6 6-3</p>
<p>Alberto Martin (Spain) beat Filip Dewulf (Belgium) 3-6 7-3 (7-3) 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>Jeff Tarango (U.S.) beat Hernan Gumy (Argentina) 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Jacobo Diaz (Spain) beat 13-Marc Rosset (Switzerland) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Paul Haarhuis (Netherlands) beat Hendrik Dreekmann (Germany) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Andrei Medvedev (Ukraine) beat Mark Knowles (Bahamas) 7-5 4-6 6-0</p>
<p>Sjeng Schalken (Netherlands) beat Javier Sanchez (Spain) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Francisco Clavet (Spain) beat Marcos Gorriz (Spain) 7-5 6-4</p>
<p>Alex Corretja (Spain) beat David Prinosil (Germany) 6-1 6-3</p>
<p>Richard Fromberg (Australia) beat Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil) 7-6 (7-4) 6-3</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>1-Thomas Muster (Austria) beat Radulescu 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Hicham Arazi (Morocco) beat Marcello Craca (Germany) 7-6 (7-1) 7-5</p>
<p>Mantilla beat Carretero 6-1 6-1</p>
<p>8-Boris Becker (Germany) beat Nicolas Kiefer (Germany) 7-5 6-2</p>
<p>Tommy Haas (Germany beat 4-Carlos Moya (Spain) 6-4 6-1</p>
<p>Gross beat Carlos Costa 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Berasategui beat Gustafsson 6-1 6-1</p>
<p>5-Marcelo Rios (Chile) beat Ruud 6-1 7-5</p>
<p>Slava Dosedel (Czech Republic) beat 16-Michael Stich (Germany) 7-6 (7-2) 6-2</p>
<p>2-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) beat Fromberg 7-6 (7-4) 7-6 (7-4)</p>
</text>
